WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:01.980
Meow.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.480
Is that right?

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.480
See? That's cute!

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.610
Yes. Cat ears are your time, Fujiwara,
as to Shinomiya is me.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.320
I know, right?

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.240
In other words,

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:21.200
the time you brought was originally
Shinomiya and cat ears alone.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.250
You're scaring me!

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>Cat ears and girls!</i>

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.880
<i>Mutualism!</i>

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.880
<i>There are relationships in this world
that are naturally symbiotic.</i>

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.760
<i>Clovers and honeybees!</i>

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.260
<i>Crocodiles and hummingbirds!</i>

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.010
<i>Avocados and soy sauce!</i>

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.510
<i>And cats...</i>

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.390
<i>Cats, which a great majority
of humans love.</i>

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.940
<i>And here we have Kaguya Shinomiya,
a graceful girl.</i>

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.980
<i>How will the compatibility
of those two things be reflected in him?</i>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.110
<i>Cute!</i>

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.740
MIRACULOUS COMPATIBILITY (MARRIAGE)

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.910
<i>A marriage!</i>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.460
KAGUYA WANTS AFFECTION

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.000
Is it really necessary to cosplay
for the welcome party?

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.000
FRENCH EXCHANGE STUDENT
WELCOME SCHEDULE

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.000
Yes!

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.550
France is the biggest cosplaying nation
right after Japan.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.260
With cosplaying, you don't need words.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.340
There's no better way
to overcome the language barrier

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.300
and deepen our friendship!

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.260
But still...

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.350
What do you think, President?

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.390
<i>Cute!</i>

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.350
MIRACULOUS COMPATIBILITY (MARRIAGE)

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.350
<i>A marriage!</i>

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:51.980
Well...

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.360
<i>Cute!</i>

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.690
Not bad, I guess.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.860
<i>No good! Whenever I look at Shinomiya,
my face tenses up!</i>

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.700
<i>I need to calm down and look normal!</i>

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.370
That's a scary look!

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.750
<i>Not much of a reaction.</i>

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.750
<i>It looks like this kind of thing
doesn't suit me.</i>

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.760
<i>It'd probably look better on someone
with more charm, like Miss Fujiwara.</i>

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.840
Wh-What is it?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:17.760
What's what?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.470
You wear a pair, too, President.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.050
<i>Meow.</i>

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.720
MEOW

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.720
How can I put it? Um...

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.430
Pointless.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.140
You don't hold back, do you?

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.980
You knew beforehand
that this wouldn't look good on me.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.020
True!

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.070
<i>Cuuute!</i>

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.490
MIRACULOUS COMPATIBILITY (MARRIAGE)

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.490
<i>A marriage!</i>

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.910
<i>What? The president just has cat ears on!</i>

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.000
<i>The reaction of others aside,
it was a perfect combo in Kaguya's mind!</i>

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.000
<i>What should I do?
I can't get my mouth to stop smiling!</i>

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.000
<i>It'll be obvious to him
that I think he looks cute!</i>

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.510
What's wrong, Shinomiya?

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.760
<i>Since it's come to this...</i>

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.390
Oh, it's nothing.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.390
<i>Skill... Biting one's tongue!</i>

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.390
<i>But that's not a perfect method.</i>

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.900
GRIN GRIN

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.900
<i>A half-grin remained on her face.</i>

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.820
SHIVER SHIVER

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.400
What's the smirk for, Shinomiya?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.820
Is there something
you'd like to say about my cat ears?

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.280
No, not at all.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.280
GRIN GRIN

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.910
They look...

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.160
very good on you.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:28.910
<i>That expression!</i>

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.660
<i>As if looking at a bug!</i>

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.790
<i>Does it mean I look so terrible
that I barely qualify as human?</i>

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.290
Miss Fujiwara,
let's take a photo of the president.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.300
Good idea!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:45.010
We have to preserve this moment
for future generations.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.010
<i>She means for extortion!</i>

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.890
<i>She'll put it away and use it
as a bargaining chip someday!</i>

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.770
Forget about it!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.430
Don't be like that.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:54.890
Kaguya, you, too.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:55.900
Me, too?

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.150
Shinomiya, too?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.150
<i>If she takes my photo,
she'll have me by the short hairs.</i>

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.150
<i>But...</i>

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.780
<i>at the same time, I'll legally be able
to obtain a cute photo of her like this!</i>

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.280
<i>A balanced scale!</i>

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.040
BALANCED SCALE

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.030
<i>The weight of the merit
and demerit are the same!</i>

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.540
If you're going to take it,
do it now, Fujiwara!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.040
<i>Shirogane chooses the cute side.</i>

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.800
<i>A side he would normally never choose!</i>

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:26.630
O-Oh. Take it with the 4K thing!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.550
R-Right!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.970
<i>Damn it! She's even cuter
when I'm standing right next to her!</i>

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.060
<i>The muscles in my face are stiffening!</i>

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.730
<i>I can't believe that looks so good on him.</i>

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.900
<i>No! My mouth is smiling by itself again!</i>

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.020
C-Could both of you
give me a cheerful smile?

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.280
- I can't!
- I can't!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.780
<i>I want to get closer to his cuteness!</i>

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.780
<i>I have to burn this image into my memory
from a shorter distance!</i>

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.280
Why are you glaring at each other?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.040
If you're going to fight,
I'm going to confiscate these!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.040
NAB

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.670
<i>What was I doing?</i>

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.420
<i>I feel like I was possessed.</i>

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.430
<i>Scary!</i>

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.180
CAT EARS ARE SCARY

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.180
<i>- Cat ears are scary!
- Cat ears are scary!</i>

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:19.190
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:
FUJIWARA LOSES

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.560
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.100
<i>Fujiwara loses.</i>

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.190
HENCEFORTH, ALL MEMBERS
OF STUDENT COUNCIL
ARE BANNED FROM WEARING CAT EARS

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.190
Um, the welcome party is next Monday.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.200
Other than making decorations, we need
to go shopping for souvenir sweets.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.200
THE STUDENT COUNCIL
WANTS IT TO BE SAID

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.450
We probably need two people for that.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.410
We'll need a few other things, too,

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.460
and enough for all of the participants,
so that's a lot of stuff.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.170
Which means giving up our day off
to go shopping.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.170
What a pain.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.170
Boy, what a pain.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.340
Who'd wanna do that?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:49.970
You know, Shinomiya?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.640
Well, true.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.390
We'll be in trouble
if no one wants to do it.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.480
Well, if it's really necessary, I could do it.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.480
FIDGET FIDGET

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:00.560
Oh!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.020
Why don't we play a game,
and the losers have to go?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.520
- A game?
- A game?

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.570
Yes! The banned word game!

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.280
THE BANNED WORD GAME

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.280
<i>The banned word game.</i>

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:12.530
Yes!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.120
Here's an example!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.540
I write a word like this
and pass it to the person on my right.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.750
Hold it up and don't look at it.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.080
SIMPLE

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.170
That's the word that person can't say.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.010
I get it. So you don't know
what your own banned word is.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:29.720
Simple.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.090
You're out!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.390
Okay, let's do it for real!

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.520
I pass it to the person on my right.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.390
In that case...

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.730
<i>I should write a word
that Fujiwara would be likely to say.</i>

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:49.360
<i>But the second and third place people
will go shopping.</i>

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.900
FIRST PLACE DOESN'T GO
SECOND AND THIRD PLACE GO

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.700
<i>Well, a man is needed
for the physical labor,</i>

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.700
STRONGER
(THAN WOMEN)

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.160
<i>while no one knows more
about traditional sweets than Shinomiya.</i>

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.160
CERTIFIED TEA EXPERT
KNOWLEDGEABLE

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.790
<i>It's just a matter of efficiency.</i>

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.540
<i>Therefore, I need to let Fujiwara win
while I beat Shinomiya.</i>

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:03.790
FIRST PLACE: FUJIWARA
SECOND PLACE: ME
THIRD PLACE: SHINOMIYA

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.050
CHECK-IT-OUT

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.050
<i>I'm sure Fujiwara would never say this!</i>

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.050
<i>I'll win for sure!</i>

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.050
CHECK-IT-OUT

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.050
All right, are we ready?

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.730
Yo, yo, let's get started, yo!

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.020
Fujiwara?

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.150
When I play da banned word game,

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.030
people always be choosin' words n' phrases
I be sayin', but not now, yo!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:35.610
I be changin' da way I speak,
so my words be different, yo! Too bad, man!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.120
<i>No!</i>

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.120
<i>Don't look at her!
I don't want her to lose!</i>

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.120
Yo, yo, yo, yo, yo, yo!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.120
<i>Crap, she'll end up saying, "check-it-out."</i>

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:48.130
Kaguya, what ya think your word is, yo?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.750
Say "Hooo!"

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.760
Say "Hooo!"

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.760
Say "Hooo"...

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.510
<i>That's childish!</i>

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.640
<i>There's a surefire way to win this game.</i>

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.140
<i>That's by not talking at all!</i>

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.900
Say "Yay!" Say "Yay!"

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.020
Shinomiya...

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.020
Say "Yay!"

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.610
We won't get anywhere like that.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.240
At the bare minimum,
speak enough to make it a conversation.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:16.780
If you insist.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.320
Fine.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.280
<i>Inevitable behavior.</i>

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.280
INEVITABLE BEHAVIOR

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:25.000
<i>"That person would do this."
"This person would say this."</i>

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.580
<i>This game produces a situation that draws
the designated word out of your opponent.</i>

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:31.800
<i>But how am I going to get her
to say that banned word?</i>

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.800
LOVE

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.760
<i>My instinct is telling me, "You've spent
half a year trying to get her to say that!</i>

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.380
<i>It's impossible!"</i>

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.800
LOVE

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.090
<i>But wait!</i>

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:41.680
<i>I can steer the conversation towards
something that Shinomiya loves doing.</i>

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.310
Fujiwara,

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.310
is there something you hate?

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.440
<i>Shirogane passed
the word "hate" on to Fujiwara,</i>

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.440
<i>a word that can easily
be connected to "love."</i>

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.320
What I hate?

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.070
Let's see.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:00.320
People often tell me I'm not good
at reading a situation, yo.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.290
But they also say that's a good thing, yo.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.960
But when they talk about love and stuff,
they don't include me!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.550
They say I'd be sure
to step on a land mine!

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.050
<i>That's sound judgment.</i>

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.680
When I think about making problems
for people without even realizing it,

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.050
it makes me sad.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.560
That's what I hate.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.140
Miss Fujiwara...

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.030
I've never thought
you've caused problems for me.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.440
In fact,

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.530
there are many people who've been helped
by your straightforwardness.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:42.580
Kaguya...

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:44.910
Really?

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.830
You don't hate me?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.920
Well, I mean... I...

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:53.590
love you.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.460
You're out, yo!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.220
LOVE

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:01.970
<i>Inevitable behavior!</i>

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.010
<i>When all is said and done,
it was inevitable...</i>

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.810
<i>that caring Kaguya would try
to comfort a depressed Fujiwara!</i>

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:09.850
<i>Fujiwara read that.</i>

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.350
<i>That was nasty!</i>

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.610
Was all that a lie?

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.990
It wasn't a lie, but a bluff, yo!

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:22.240
Of course people would include me
in conversations about love interests, yo!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.910
<i>Since we've gotten this far,
the rest should be easy.</i>

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.870
<i>I'll lose automatically by letting
my guard down and following her lead.</i>

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.790
<i>She's got everything she needs to win.</i>

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.000
<i>But...</i>

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.670
Hey, when it rains, it pours, yo!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:33.920
<i>was that the truth?</i>

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.040
<i>She said it was a bluff,</i>

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.590
<i>but a bluff has power because
it's a pinch of a lie mixed with truth.</i>

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.590
It must be nice, having no troubles.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.590
<i>If that's the case,
how much of it was a lie?</i>

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.430
<i>When Fujiwara was speaking
about feeling alienated,</i>

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.520
<i>were those words and her eyes all lies?</i>

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.850
<i>If it's possible that they weren't...</i>

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.480
<i>then, I'm playing this game wrong.</i>

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.110
<i>I can't stand the idea of hurting others
for the sake of my own self-interest.</i>

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.530
<i>That's my credo,
and this situation relates to it.</i>

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:06.280
<i>Prioritizing my own circumstances
and purposely losing...</i>

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.540
<i>That would be self-interest
and truly alienate her!</i>

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:12.160
<i>The idea of going out shopping
with Shinomiya may be appealing,</i>

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.290
<i>but...</i>

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.540
<i>I can't betray my own conviction!</i>

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.130
Fujiwara...

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.050
I'm going to get serious here!

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.800
You're out, yo!

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.970
Yes! I beat the president, too!

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.730
Yay! Yay!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.850
<i>Inevitable behavior.</i>

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:37.650
<i>An action a person would necessarily take
given certain circumstances.</i>

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:39.190
SERIOUS

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:41.940
<i>And predicting that
is the essential point of the game.</i>

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.070
Shopping, huh?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.700
Well, we lost,
so I guess we can't complain.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:53.710
<i>The banned word game is a game that
demands understanding of your opponents.</i>

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.210
Ah, dammit.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.790
I lost.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.750
We're going to buy the souvenirs.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.010
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:
UTTER DEFEAT FOR SHIROGANE

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.720
<i>Results of today's match...
Utter defeat for Shirogane.</i>

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.670
All right! I'm looking forward
to seeing what you get, yo!

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.720
THE HEART THROBBING
SHOPPING ARC CONTINUES

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.970
CHECK-IT-OUT

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:06.970
"Check-it-out"?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:12.140
The president said we'd talk
about shopping after he got back.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:12.850
Oh.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.190
The day he bought a smartphone,

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.860
we exchanged e-mail addresses
and phone numbers.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.940
But I've been waiting and waiting,
and he still hasn't contacted me!

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.860
He has no intention
of sending me a message first!

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:27.110
"President, I'm looking forward
to tomorrow—"

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.700
What are you doing?

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.490
Well, I thought
I'd send a text on your behalf.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:35.370
Don't! I'm not sending the first text!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:37.080
KAGUYA WANTS HIM TO SEND IT

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.080
All this beating around the bush...

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.500
Lady Kaguya, you're in love
with President Shirogane, aren't you?

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:46.760
I have feelings for the president.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.090
Then...

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:54.520
But I'm only interested
because he's got the elements I lack.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:57.520
It's definitely not love.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:01.020
Then, what if the secretary started
dating President Shirogane?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:05.780
Well?

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.360
You've got it wrong!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.450
I wouldn't want the president
to take Miss Fujiwara away from me!

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.290
Despite appearances,
she's my dear friend.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.410
From: Fujiwara
Subject: Octopus
Look! A live octopus!!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.420
She's your dear friend, right?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.670
If it weighs on your mind that much,

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:23.800
Lady Kaguya...

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.170
instead of a text, why not call?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.880
C-Call?

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.890
He's expecting a text.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.100
Exploit that carelessness,
and attack this way!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.890
Carelessness? Attack?

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.100
It's the perfect plan.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.610
Before Lady Kaguya quibbles about it,
click-click there.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.110
Here you go.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.110
Wait! I'm not mentally prepared!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.030
SHIROGANE

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.030
RINGING

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.030
<i>Hello?</i>

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.700
This is Shinomiya.

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.410
President, is that you?

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.910
I'm Miyuki's father.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:03.170
<i>U-Um, is the president...
I mean, is Shirogane there?</i>

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.590
I am Shirogane.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.630
<i>No, I mean...</i>

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.130
i-is Miyuki there?

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.800
<i>Oh, my son?</i>

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:13.760
<i>Miyuki! A girl's on the phone for you!</i>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.310
<i>A girl's calling for him?</i>

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:19.390
<i>Wha... You don't answer
another person's cell phone, Dad!</i>

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.150
It's me.

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:25.520
It's Shinomiya.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.030
<i>Oh, Shinomiya?</i>

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.700
I was calling about the plan for tomorrow.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.240
Is now okay?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:32.910
<i>Sure.</i>

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.160
I'm in the tub, but that's fine.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.040
The tub?

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.620
Then he's naked, huh?

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:43.040
Lady Kaguya, right now you're talking
to someone who's completely exposed.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.040
<i>It's muffled on your end.</i>

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.170
I-I'll call you back!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:46.800
<i>No problem.</i>

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.170
My phone is waterproof.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.050
<i>There is a problem.</i>

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.640
How about we meet tomorrow
at 11 am in front of Hachiko?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:55.800
<i>Okay.</i>

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.810
We'll buy the sweets, then go to Hands.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.520
I guess that's about it.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.310
Right.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:04.060
STRETCH OUT THE CONVERSATION MORE

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.310
<i>Well, I'll see you tomorrow.</i>

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:04.060
Yes.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:05.520
<i>Shinomiya—</i>

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.820
What? What were you about to say?

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.080
I'm going to sleep.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:21.330
FROM: SHIROGANE
I WAS TRYING TO TELL YOU SOMETHING
AS YOU HUNG UP THE PHONE

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.920
LOOKS LIKE TONIGHT WILL GET PRETTY COLD,
SO BE WARM AND GO TO SLEEP
GOOD NIGHT

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.550
Good for you. Your first text.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:31.510
<i>Results of today's match... Kaguya wins.</i>

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:31.920
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:
KAGUYA WINS

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.430
THE NEXT DAY

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.430
It seems Shibuya Station is flooded.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.180
I'm going.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.270
The president is waiting for me.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.770
I have to go!

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.190
There's no way he's there.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.700
A text canceling our plans...

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.450
But it's the first text
Shinomiya has sent me, right?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.500
So I'll call that a win for today.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.580
Thankfully, my phone is waterproof.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:08.590
THE END OF THE HEART THROBBING
SHOPPING ARC

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:11.960
TOOK 30 MINUTES
TO SEND THE CANCELLATION TEXT.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.550
FRENCH FOREIGN EXCHANGE STUDENTS
WELCOME PARTY

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:17.800
We got it ready in time!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.180
Good work, everyone!

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:24.810
Headmaster, next time,
please don't tell us so last-minute.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:26.150
MIYUKI SHIROGANE WANTS TO TALK

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.690
Understood!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:30.270
Well, everyone, have a good time!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.450
Can you speak French, Shinomiya?

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.570
No. Not very well.

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:39.070
How about you, President?

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.710
I AM MIYUKI SHIROGANE

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.670
You're not the president for nothing.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.340
I just prepared by studying the handbook.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.470
U-Um...

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.480
<i>Liar!</i>

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.950
You can speak French?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.070
Yes!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.330
My mom is a former diplomat,

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.870
so ever since I was little, she drummed
various languages into my head.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.580
<i>Wait a second.</i>

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:32.420
<i>Am I the only person here
who can't speak French?</i>

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.920
COMPLETELY ISOLATED

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.920
<i>He's completely isolated!</i>

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.970
<i>Wh-Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.430
<i>If they figure out
I'm the only one who doesn't speak it...</i>

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:43.850
<i>President of student council
of a Japanese school can't speak French?</i>

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.930
<i>Maybe he's just dumb.</i>

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.320
HOW CUTE...

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.820
<i>This is bad, bad for my heart.</i>

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:58.700
<i>Shirogane...</i>

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:03.700
<i>why do you think I suddenly asked you
to prepare a party?</i>

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:05.740
<i>I must determine...</i>

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:09.210
<i>whether you're truly someone
to whom this academy can be entrusted.</i>

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.460
<i>The real test begins now.</i>

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.800
Betsy...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.340
Yes.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.300
No need to go easy on him.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:23.430
Make mincemeat out of Miyuki Shirogane
with everything you've got.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.640
Are you sure?

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:28.980
<i>Betsy Beltoise, the vice-president
of the French school's student council.</i>

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.810
<i>Her nickname is "The Wound-licking Razor."</i>

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:36.730
THE WOUND-LICKING RAZOR

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:35.980
<i>No one has ever been impervious
to her verbal attack.</i>

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.730
VERBAL ATTACK

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.450
Hey.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.830
<i>Betsy's sarcasm is like punching
someone you've just met in the face.</i>

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:54.080
<i>Next, she provokes him as if simultaneously
insulting his parents and lover.</i>

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.260
<i>On top of that,
she diminishes his character</i>

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:04.090
<i>in a way that would make
a man in his sixties break down in tears.</i>

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.100
THAT'S IT!

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:10.600
<i>Miyuki Shirogane!</i>

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:14.730
<i>He smiles confidently in the face
of that merciless verbal onslaught?</i>

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:17.610
<i>I'd be throwing up
while bowing down on the ground!</i>

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:22.110
<i>You'd think he couldn't comprehend
what she was saying!</i>

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.200
<i>My verbal assault isn't getting through!</i>

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.870
<i>That's impossible!</i>

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:30.870
<i>Betsy unleashes even stronger invective
against Shirogane.</i>

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.010
What was that?

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.010
You...

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:47.100
Oh, sorry.
You don't understand Japanese, do you?

00:20:56.360 --> 00:21:01.030
<i>Kaguya menaces Betsy with language that'd
get the attention of the Broadcasting Code.</i>

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.540
Shinomiya?

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:11.580
P-President!

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.290
Don't get the wrong idea! That was...

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.130
She... She's going to kill me!

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:18.790
I'm sorry. I-It's okay.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:22.050
Japanese high school girls are scary!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.090
<i>Oh, what did I do?</i>

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:27.800
<i>Exhibition match. The Japanese school won.</i>

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:27.800
EXHIBITION MATCH
THE JAPANESE SCHOOL WON

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.310
I bet you look down on me now.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:40.440
After being so foul-mouthed...

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:44.820
This is like the old me.

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:49.530
Like I said at the beginning,
I skimmed the French handbook.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.330
I couldn't have caught what you said.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.830
So, I have no idea
what you were saying to her.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:22:00.170
I just know you were mad
because she was badmouthing me.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.340
Thank you.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:04.630
President!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:07.840
That's one thing I...

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:11.720
...about you.

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:14.350
What?

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:15.730
What did you say?

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.270
It's a secret.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:19.230
Hey, don't do that to me!

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:20.860
It only makes me wanna know more!

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:22.440
A secret is a secret.

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:23.730
What did you say?

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:24.570
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:25.490
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:
BOTH WINNERS

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:25.240
It wasn't in French.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:26.990
<i>Both winners.</i>

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.990
- In Latin?
- No.

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:29.200
BECAUSE THEY SHOWED
EACH OTHER THEIR WEAKNESS

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.450
- In Yiddish?
- No.

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:29.950
- In Finnish?
- No.
